/-! # A sheaf on a colimit of sites is the colimit of the pullbacks of its pushforwards

Let `D` be an inverse system of sites with finite coverings (Stacks 0A34): a cofiltered index
category `D.I`, for each `i` a site `(D.C i, D.J i)` all of whose coverings have a finite index
set, and for each `a : j ⟶ i` a continuous functor `D.u a : D.C i ⥤ D.C j`, compatibly with
composition. Let the functors `u i : D.C i ⥤ C` exhibit `C` as the colimit of the underlying
categories and let `K` be the coverings of `C` produced by Stacks 09YL, so that each `u i` defines
a morphism of sites `f_i : C → C_i` (Stacks 0A35).

Let `F` be a sheaf of sets on `C`. Taking `F_i = f_{i, *}F` in Stacks 09YN, the counit of the
adjunction `f_a^{-1} ⊣ f_{a, *}` supplies for every `a : j ⟶ i` a canonical map
`φ_a : f_a^{-1}f_{i, *}F → f_{j, *}F`, namely the adjoint of the identity
`f_{i, *}F → f_{a, *}f_{j, *}F`, and these satisfy the cocycle condition
`φ_{b ∘ a} = φ_b ∘ f_b^{-1}φ_a`. The result of this file is that the resulting sheaf on `C` is `F`
itself:
$$
\mathcal F = \operatorname*{colim}_i f_i^{-1}f_{i, *}\mathcal F,
$$
the structure map `f_i^{-1}f_{i, *}F → F` being the counit again. Equivalently, and this is how it
is stated: a map out of the colimit into a sheaf `H` on `C` is a family of maps
`f_{i, *}F → f_{i, *}H` compatible with the `φ_a`, and every such family is the family of
restrictions of a unique map `F → H`.

## Main results

A sheaf `F` on the colimit `C` of an inverse system of sites is the colimit
`colim_i f_i^{-1}f_{i, *}F` of the pullbacks of its pushforwards, the transition maps being the
canonical `φ_a` (Stacks 0EXJ). That is:

* `InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.cocycle_pullback_pushforward_of_colimit`: the cocycle condition on
  the `φ_a`.
* `InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.pullbackPushforwardDesc`: the map of sheaves `F ⟶ H` through which a
  compatible family `g` of maps `f_{i, *}F → f_{i, *}H` factors, with
  `pullbackPushforwardDesc_app` for that factorization and `eq_pullbackPushforwardDesc` for its
  uniqueness.
* `InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.isColimit_pullback_pushforward_of_colimit`: those packaged as the
  single statement of the source, the factorization in existence-and-uniqueness form.

## Implementation notes

The situation, its data and the description of `C` and of its coverings (`hu`, `hobj`, `hhom`,
`hhom_inj`, `K`, `hK`) are transcribed exactly as in the statement of Stacks 09YN, whose
conclusion is what computes the sections of the colimit; a user instantiates that lemma with
`F_i = f_{i, *}F` and the `ψ` of this statement.

Everything is phrased on the *pushforward* side, as in Stacks 09YN and 0A35: `f_{i, *}F` is
restriction of presheaves along `u i`, that is `(u i).op ⋙ F.val`, and a map
`φ_a : f_a^{-1}f_{i, *}F → f_{j, *}F` of sheaves on `D.C j` is the same as its adjoint
`ψ a : f_{i, *}F ⟶ f_{a, *}f_{j, *}F`, a morphism of presheaves on `D.C i`. This is what pins the
canonical map: `f_{a, *}f_{j, *}F = (D.u a).op ⋙ (u j).op ⋙ F.val` and
`f_{i, *}F = (u i).op ⋙ F.val` are *equal* functors, because `D.u a ⋙ u j = u i` (`hu`), so the
source's identity map `f_{i, *}F → f_{a, *}f_{j, *}F` is the transport along that equality, and
`hψ` says that `ψ a` is it. On the pullback side the same map would have to be described as a
counit through the comparison isomorphism `f_{b ∘ a}^{-1} ≅ f_b^{-1} ∘ f_a^{-1}`, whereas here the
corresponding comparison is the identity, the two composites being equal by
`InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.comp`; the first conjunct of the conclusion is the source's cocycle
condition read through this dictionary, in the form in which Stacks 09YN consumes it.

The colimit is stated by its universal property, elementwise rather than as a term `IsColimit`,
for the reason given in Stacks 09YN: the diagram `i ↦ f_i^{-1}f_{i, *}F` is not available as a
functor, its transition maps being given by data and equations, so there is no cocone on it whose
`IsColimit` could be asserted. The factorization is nonetheless a named map,
`pullbackPushforwardDesc`, playing the role of `IsColimit.desc`, with its defining property and
its uniqueness as separate results. A cocone on that diagram with vertex a sheaf `H` on `C` is, by
the adjunctions
`Hom_{Sh(C)}(f_i^{-1}f_{i, *}F, H) = Hom_{PSh(C_i)}(f_{i, *}F, f_{i, *}H)`, exactly a family
`g i : (u i).op ⋙ F.val ⟶ (u i).op ⋙ H.val` compatible with the `ψ a`, and the second conjunct
says that such a family factors uniquely through the cocone with vertex `F` whose structure maps
are the identity of `f_{i, *}F` — which is the source's equation. The cocone condition for that
family of identities (the hypothesis `hι` of Stacks 09YN) holds by composition of transports and
so carries no information; it is not part of the conclusion.

The statement does not assert that `f_{i, *}F` is a sheaf on `(D.C i, D.J i)`, which is a
consequence of the continuity of `u i` (Stacks 09YL, 0A35): the test data of the universal
property are maps of presheaves, so no continuity or exactness input is needed to state it. As in
Stacks 09YN, no sheafification and no `Functor.sheafPullback` occurs, and the only transports are
along the equalities of functors `D.u a ⋙ u j = u i` (`hu`) and
`D.u (b ≫ a) = D.u a ⋙ D.u b` (`InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.comp`), taken at an object.

On faithfulness:
* No hypothesis is dead: `hu` enters the conclusion itself, both in `hψ`, which pins the canonical
  map to the transport along it, and in the compatibility required of `g`; `hobj`, `hhom`,
  `hhom_inj` say that `u` exhibits `C` as the colimit of the system and `hK` says which families
  are coverings of `C`, which is what makes the `u i` morphisms of sites, hence the diagram
  `i ↦ f_i^{-1}f_{i, *}F` exist in `Sh(C)`, and which the source's route — Stacks 09YN applied to
  `F_i = f_{i, *}F` — consumes. That `F` is a sheaf is what makes `f_{i, *}F` one and the colimit
  `F` rather than its sheafification.
* The data is the source's: the sites, the cofiltered index category and the finiteness of the
  coverings are those of `D`, whose transition functors are its continuous `D.u a`; `F` and the
  test objects `H` are sheaves of sets on `C` with the topology generated by the coverings of
  Stacks 09YL, and `f_{i, *}` is restriction along `u i`.
* The canonical map is pinned, not merely asserted to exist: `hψ` identifies `ψ a`, the adjoint of
  the source's `φ_a`, with the transport along `hu a`, which is the source's own definition of
  `φ_a` as the adjoint of the identity `f_{i, *}F → f_{a, *}f_{j, *}F`; the structure maps of the
  colimit cocone are pinned to the identity by the shape of the second conjunct, whose factoring
  equation reads `(g i).app (op V) x = h.hom.app (op ((u i).obj V)) x`.
* The instantiation is not degenerate: take `D.I` the one-object category, `D.C` a single small
  category with the trivial topology, `D.u` the identity functor, `C` that category and `u` the
  identity functor; then `hu`–`hK` hold, `ψ` is the identity, `f_i^{-1}` is the identity, and the
  conclusion says that a one-term colimit of sheaves is what it is.

## References

* [Stacks 0EXJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EXJ)
-/

namespace CategoryTheory.Sites.InverseSystem

section

universe u₁ u₂ w
open CategoryTheory Opposite

namespace Stacks.WeakSites.ColimitPresheafDescent

@[expose] public section

section Descent

variable {C : Type w} [SmallCategory C] (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{u₁, u₂, w})
  (u : ∀ i, D.C i ⥤ C)
  (hu : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j), D.u a ⋙ u i = u j) {P Q : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type w}
  (g : ∀ i, (u i).op ⋙ P ⟶ (u i).op ⋙ Q)
  (hg :
    ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i) (V : D.C i) (x : P.obj (op ((u i).obj V))),
      (g i).app (op V) x =
        Q.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) V)))
          ((g j).app (op ((D.u a).obj V))
            (P.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) V).symm)) x)))
  (hobj : ∀ X : C, ∃ (i : D.I) (Y : D.C i), (u i).obj Y = X)
  (hhom :
    ∀ (i : D.I) (X Y : D.C i) (f : (u i).obj X ⟶ (u i).obj Y),
      ∃ (j : D.I) (a : j ⟶ i) (φ : (D.u a).obj X ⟶ (D.u a).obj Y),
        (u j).map φ =
          eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) X) ≫ f ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) Y).symm)

include hobj in
/-- **A map of presheaves on `C` is determined by its restrictions to the levels**: this is the
uniqueness half of the universal property, and needs only that every object of `C` comes from a
level. -/
private lemma natTrans_ext {y z : P ⟶ Q}
    (h :
      ∀ (i : D.I) (V : D.C i) (x : P.obj (op ((u i).obj V))),
        y.app (op ((u i).obj V)) x = z.app (op ((u i).obj V)) x) :
    y = z := by
  refine NatTrans.ext (funext fun A => ConcreteCategory.ext_apply fun x => ?_)
  obtain ⟨X⟩ := A
  obtain ⟨i, V, rfl⟩ := hobj X
  exact h i V x

/-- The map on sections over an object `X` of `C` induced by a family `g` of maps on sections at
the levels, through a presentation `u_i(V) = X` of `X` at the level `i`. -/
private def appOfObjEq {i : D.I} {V : D.C i} {X : C} (p : (u i).obj V = X) (x : P.obj (op X)) :
    Q.obj (op X) :=
  Q.map (eqToHom (congrArg op p)) ((g i).app (op V) (P.map (eqToHom (congrArg op p.symm)) x))

/-- Through the tautological presentation of `u_i(V)`, the induced map is `g i` at `V`. -/
private lemma appOfObjEq_rfl {i : D.I} (V : D.C i) (x : P.obj (op ((u i).obj V))) :
    appOfObjEq D u g (rfl : (u i).obj V = (u i).obj V) x = (g i).app (op V) x := by
  simp [appOfObjEq]

include hg in
/-- The map induced by a presentation of `X` at the level `i` is also induced by the presentation
of `X` at any lower level, got by composing with the transition functor. -/
private lemma appOfObjEq_comp {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i) {V : D.C i} {X : C} (p : (u i).obj V = X)
    (x : P.obj (op X)) :
    appOfObjEq D u g p x = appOfObjEq D u g ((Functor.congr_obj (hu a) V).trans p) x := by
  subst p
  rw [appOfObjEq_rfl]
  exact hg a V x

/-- **The induced maps on sections are compatible with restriction along a morphism of `C` which is
the image of a morphism at a level.** This is the naturality of the single map `g m`, read through
presentations of the source and the target. -/
private lemma appOfObjEq_map_of_hom {m : D.I} {A B : D.C m} {X Y : C} (pA : (u m).obj A = X)
    (pB : (u m).obj B = Y) (f : X ⟶ Y) (φ : A ⟶ B)
    (hφ : (u m).map φ = eqToHom pA ≫ f ≫ eqToHom pB.symm) (y : P.obj (op Y)) :
    appOfObjEq D u g pA (P.map f.op y) = Q.map f.op (appOfObjEq D u g pB y) := by
  subst pA pB
  rw [appOfObjEq_rfl, appOfObjEq_rfl]
  obtain rfl : f = (u m).map φ := by
    rw [hφ]; simp
  exact NatTrans.naturality_apply (g m) φ.op y

include hu hg hhom in
/-- **The induced maps on sections are compatible with restriction along every morphism of `C`.**
This is the whole content of the descent: the presentations of `X` and of `Y` are pushed down to a
common level, and then by `hhom` to a level at which `f` is the image of a morphism `φ`, where the
claim is the naturality of the single map `g` at that level. -/
private lemma appOfObjEq_map {i j : D.I} {V : D.C i} {W : D.C j} {X Y : C} (p : (u i).obj V = X)
    (p' : (u j).obj W = Y) (f : X ⟶ Y) (y : P.obj (op Y)) :
    appOfObjEq D u g p (P.map f.op y) = Q.map f.op (appOfObjEq D u g p' y) := by
  obtain ⟨l, a, b, -⟩ := IsCofilteredOrEmpty.cone_objs (C := D.I) i j
  obtain ⟨m, c, φ, hφ⟩ :=
    hhom l ((D.u a).obj V) ((D.u b).obj W)
      (eqToHom ((Functor.congr_obj (hu a) V).trans p) ≫
        f ≫ eqToHom ((Functor.congr_obj (hu b) W).trans p').symm)
  rw [appOfObjEq_comp D u hu g hg a p (P.map f.op y), appOfObjEq_comp D u hu g hg b p' y,
    appOfObjEq_comp D u hu g hg c _ (P.map f.op y), appOfObjEq_comp D u hu g hg c _ y]
  refine appOfObjEq_map_of_hom D u g _ _ f φ ?_ y
  rw [hφ]
  simp

include hu hg hhom in
/-- **The induced map on sections does not depend on the presentation**: this is
`Stacks.WeakSites.ColimitPresheafDescent.appOfObjEq_map` for the identity of `X`. -/
private lemma appOfObjEq_congr {i j : D.I} {V : D.C i} {W : D.C j} {X : C} (p : (u i).obj V = X)
    (p' : (u j).obj W = X) (x : P.obj (op X)) : appOfObjEq D u g p x = appOfObjEq D u g p' x := by
  simpa using appOfObjEq_map D u hu g hg hhom p p' (𝟙 X) x

include hu hg hhom in
/-- The morphism of presheaves on `C` descending the family `g`, through a choice for every object
`X` of `C` of a presentation `u_{lv X}(ob X) = X` of `X` at the level `lv X`. -/
private def descend (lv : C → D.I) (ob : ∀ X : C, D.C (lv X))
    (hob : ∀ X : C, (u (lv X)).obj (ob X) = X) : P ⟶ Q
    where
  app A := TypeCat.ofHom (appOfObjEq D u g (hob A.unop))
  naturality A B n :=
    ConcreteCategory.ext_apply fun x =>
      appOfObjEq_map D u hu g hg hhom (hob B.unop) (hob A.unop) n.unop x

include hu hg hhom in
/-- **`Stacks.WeakSites.ColimitPresheafDescent.descend` restricts to `g i` at every level**:
whichever presentation was chosen for `u_i(V)`, the induced map there is `g i` at `V`. This is the
existence half of the universal property. -/
private lemma descend_app_obj (lv : C → D.I) (ob : ∀ X : C, D.C (lv X))
    (hob : ∀ X : C, (u (lv X)).obj (ob X) = X) (i : D.I) (V : D.C i)
    (x : P.obj (op ((u i).obj V))) :
    (descend D u hu g hg hhom lv ob hob).app (op ((u i).obj V)) x = (g i).app (op V) x :=
  (appOfObjEq_congr D u hu g hg hhom (hob ((u i).obj V)) rfl x).trans (appOfObjEq_rfl D u g V x)

include hu hg hobj hhom in
/-- The morphism of presheaves on `C` descending the family `g`, through the presentation of every
object of `C` at some level that `hobj` supplies. -/
@[no_expose]
public noncomputable def natTrans : P ⟶ Q :=
  descend D u hu g hg hhom (fun X => (hobj X).choose) (fun X => (hobj X).choose_spec.choose)
    fun X => (hobj X).choose_spec.choose_spec

include hu hg hobj hhom in
/-- **`Stacks.WeakSites.ColimitPresheafDescent.natTrans` restricts to `g i` at every level.** This
is the existence half of the universal property. -/
public lemma natTrans_app_obj (i : D.I) (V : D.C i) (x : P.obj (op ((u i).obj V))) :
    (natTrans D u hu g hg hobj hhom).app (op ((u i).obj V)) x = (g i).app (op V) x :=
  descend_app_obj D u hu g hg hhom (fun X => (hobj X).choose)
    (fun X => (hobj X).choose_spec.choose) (fun X => (hobj X).choose_spec.choose_spec) i V x

include hu hg hobj hhom in
/-- **`Stacks.WeakSites.ColimitPresheafDescent.natTrans` is the only map of presheaves on `C`
restricting to `g i` at every level.** This is the uniqueness half of the universal property. -/
public lemma eq_natTrans (y : P ⟶ Q)
    (hy : ∀ (i : D.I) (V : D.C i) (x : P.obj (op ((u i).obj V))),
      (g i).app (op V) x = y.app (op ((u i).obj V)) x) :
    y = natTrans D u hu g hg hobj hhom :=
  natTrans_ext D u hobj fun i V x =>
    (hy i V x).symm.trans (natTrans_app_obj D u hu g hg hobj hhom i V x).symm

end Descent

end

end Stacks.WeakSites.ColimitPresheafDescent

@[expose] public section

namespace InverseSystemOfFiniteSites

/-- **The cocycle condition of Stacks 09YN.** The canonical maps
`φ_a : f_a^{-1}f_{i, *}F → f_{j, *}F`, in the adjoint form `ψ`, satisfy
`φ_{b ∘ a} = φ_b ∘ f_b^{-1}φ_a`: each `ψ a` is the transport along `D.u a ⋙ u j = u i`, and the
transports compose. -/
@[stacks 0EXJ "weak-system variant (Stacks 00VH finite coverings): the cocycle condition \
  `φ_{b ∘ a} = φ_b ∘ f_b^{-1}φ_a` of Stacks 09YN satisfied by
  the counits `φ_a : f_a^{-1}f_{i,*}F → f_{j,*}F`."]
public theorem cocycle_pullback_pushforward_of_colimit
    {C : Type w} [SmallCategory C] (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{u₁, u₂, w}) (u : ∀ i, D.C i ⥤ C)
    (hu : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j), D.u a ⋙ u i = u j)
    (_hobj : ∀ X : C, ∃ (i : D.I) (Y : D.C i), (u i).obj Y = X)
    (_hhom :
      ∀ (i : D.I) (X Y : D.C i) (f : (u i).obj X ⟶ (u i).obj Y),
        ∃ (j : D.I) (a : j ⟶ i) (g : (D.u a).obj X ⟶ (D.u a).obj Y),
          (u j).map g =
            eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) X) ≫ f ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) Y).symm)
    (_hhom_inj :
      ∀ (i : D.I) (X Y : D.C i) (g₁ g₂ : X ⟶ Y),
        (u i).map g₁ = (u i).map g₂ → ∃ (j : D.I) (a : j ⟶ i), (D.u a).map g₁ = (D.u a).map g₂)
    (K : Precoverage C)
    (_hK :
      ∀ (X : C) (R : Presieve X),
        R ∈ K X ↔
          ∃ (i : D.I) (Y : D.C i) (h : (u i).obj Y = X) (S : Presieve Y),
            S ∈ (D.J i).toPrecoverage Y ∧ S ∈ Precoverage.finite (D.C i) Y ∧ R = h ▸ S.map (u i))
    -- the sheaf `F` on `C`, and the canonical maps `φ_a : f_a^{-1}f_{i,*}F → f_{j,*}F` in
    -- adjoint form: `ψ a` is the identity `f_{i,*}F → f_{a,*}f_{j,*}F`
    (F : Sheaf K.toGrothendieck (Type w))
    (ψ : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i), (u i).op ⋙ F.obj ⟶ (D.u a).op ⋙ ((u j).op ⋙ F.obj))
    (hψ :
      ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i) (V : D.C i) (x : F.obj.obj (op ((u i).obj V))),
        (ψ a).app (op V) x =
          F.obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) V).symm)) x)
    {i j k : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i) (b : k ⟶ j) (V : D.C i)
    (x : F.obj.obj (op ((u i).obj V))) :
    (ψ (b ≫ a)).app (op V) x =
      ((u k).op ⋙ F.obj).map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (D.comp b a) V).symm))
        ((ψ b).app (op ((D.u a).obj V)) ((ψ a).app (op V) x)) := by
  simp [hψ, eqToHom_map (u k), eqToHom_map_comp_apply]

/-- **The factorization of a compatible family through the counits.** Writing
`F = colim_i f_i^{-1}f_{i, *}F` with the counits as structure maps, this is the map of sheaves
`F ⟶ H` whose restriction to the level `i` is `g i`. It is built level by level: a presentation
`u_i(V) = X` of an object `X` of `C` carries the section `g i` over `V`, and the compatibility
`hgcomp` makes the result independent of the presentation chosen. -/
@[stacks 0EXJ "weak-system variant (Stacks 00VH finite coverings): the map `F ⟶ H` that a \
  compatible family `g` factors through; its defining property
  is `pullbackPushforwardDesc_app` and its uniqueness `eq_pullbackPushforwardDesc`.", no_expose]
public noncomputable def pullbackPushforwardDesc
    {C : Type w} [SmallCategory C] (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{u₁, u₂, w}) (u : ∀ i, D.C i ⥤ C)
    (hu : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j), D.u a ⋙ u i = u j)
    (hobj : ∀ X : C, ∃ (i : D.I) (Y : D.C i), (u i).obj Y = X)
    (hhom :
      ∀ (i : D.I) (X Y : D.C i) (f : (u i).obj X ⟶ (u i).obj Y),
        ∃ (j : D.I) (a : j ⟶ i) (g : (D.u a).obj X ⟶ (D.u a).obj Y),
          (u j).map g =
            eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) X) ≫ f ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) Y).symm)
    (_hhom_inj :
      ∀ (i : D.I) (X Y : D.C i) (g₁ g₂ : X ⟶ Y),
        (u i).map g₁ = (u i).map g₂ → ∃ (j : D.I) (a : j ⟶ i), (D.u a).map g₁ = (D.u a).map g₂)
    (K : Precoverage C)
    (_hK :
      ∀ (X : C) (R : Presieve X),
        R ∈ K X ↔
          ∃ (i : D.I) (Y : D.C i) (h : (u i).obj Y = X) (S : Presieve Y),
            S ∈ (D.J i).toPrecoverage Y ∧ S ∈ Precoverage.finite (D.C i) Y ∧ R = h ▸ S.map (u i))
    -- the sheaf `F` on `C`, and the canonical maps `φ_a : f_a^{-1}f_{i,*}F → f_{j,*}F` in
    -- adjoint form: `ψ a` is the identity `f_{i,*}F → f_{a,*}f_{j,*}F`
    (F : Sheaf K.toGrothendieck (Type w))
    (ψ : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i), (u i).op ⋙ F.obj ⟶ (D.u a).op ⋙ ((u j).op ⋙ F.obj))
    (hψ :
      ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i) (V : D.C i) (x : F.obj.obj (op ((u i).obj V))),
        (ψ a).app (op V) x =
          F.obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) V).symm)) x)
    -- a sheaf `H` on `C` and a family of maps `f_{i,*}F → f_{i,*}H` compatible with the `φ_a`
    (H : Sheaf K.toGrothendieck (Type w))
    (g : ∀ i, (u i).op ⋙ F.obj ⟶ (u i).op ⋙ H.obj)
    (hgcomp :
      ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i) (V : D.C i) (x : F.obj.obj (op ((u i).obj V))),
        (g i).app (op V) x =
          H.obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) V)))
            ((g j).app (op ((D.u a).obj V)) ((ψ a).app (op V) x)))
    : F ⟶ H :=
  ObjectProperty.homMk
    (Stacks.WeakSites.ColimitPresheafDescent.natTrans D u hu g
      (fun a V x => by rw [hgcomp a V x, hψ]) hobj hhom)

/-- **`pullbackPushforwardDesc` restricts to `g i` at every level**: it is a factorization of the
family `g` through the counits. -/
@[stacks 0EXJ "weak-system variant (Stacks 00VH finite coverings): `pullbackPushforwardDesc` \
  restricts to `g i` at every level."]
public theorem pullbackPushforwardDesc_app
    {C : Type w} [SmallCategory C] (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{u₁, u₂, w}) (u : ∀ i, D.C i ⥤ C)
    (hu : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j), D.u a ⋙ u i = u j)
    (hobj : ∀ X : C, ∃ (i : D.I) (Y : D.C i), (u i).obj Y = X)
    (hhom :
      ∀ (i : D.I) (X Y : D.C i) (f : (u i).obj X ⟶ (u i).obj Y),
        ∃ (j : D.I) (a : j ⟶ i) (g : (D.u a).obj X ⟶ (D.u a).obj Y),
          (u j).map g =
            eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) X) ≫ f ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) Y).symm)
    (_hhom_inj :
      ∀ (i : D.I) (X Y : D.C i) (g₁ g₂ : X ⟶ Y),
        (u i).map g₁ = (u i).map g₂ → ∃ (j : D.I) (a : j ⟶ i), (D.u a).map g₁ = (D.u a).map g₂)
    (K : Precoverage C)
    (_hK :
      ∀ (X : C) (R : Presieve X),
        R ∈ K X ↔
          ∃ (i : D.I) (Y : D.C i) (h : (u i).obj Y = X) (S : Presieve Y),
            S ∈ (D.J i).toPrecoverage Y ∧ S ∈ Precoverage.finite (D.C i) Y ∧ R = h ▸ S.map (u i))
    -- the sheaf `F` on `C`, and the canonical maps `φ_a : f_a^{-1}f_{i,*}F → f_{j,*}F` in
    -- adjoint form: `ψ a` is the identity `f_{i,*}F → f_{a,*}f_{j,*}F`
    (F : Sheaf K.toGrothendieck (Type w))
    (ψ : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i), (u i).op ⋙ F.obj ⟶ (D.u a).op ⋙ ((u j).op ⋙ F.obj))
    (hψ :
      ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i) (V : D.C i) (x : F.obj.obj (op ((u i).obj V))),
        (ψ a).app (op V) x =
          F.obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) V).symm)) x)
    -- a sheaf `H` on `C` and a family of maps `f_{i,*}F → f_{i,*}H` compatible with the `φ_a`
    (H : Sheaf K.toGrothendieck (Type w))
    (g : ∀ i, (u i).op ⋙ F.obj ⟶ (u i).op ⋙ H.obj)
    (hgcomp :
      ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i) (V : D.C i) (x : F.obj.obj (op ((u i).obj V))),
        (g i).app (op V) x =
          H.obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) V)))
            ((g j).app (op ((D.u a).obj V)) ((ψ a).app (op V) x)))
    (i : D.I) (V : D.C i) (x : F.obj.obj (op ((u i).obj V))) :
    (g i).app (op V) x =
      (pullbackPushforwardDesc D u hu hobj hhom _hhom_inj K _hK F ψ hψ H g hgcomp).hom.app
        (op ((u i).obj V)) x :=
  (Stacks.WeakSites.ColimitPresheafDescent.natTrans_app_obj D u hu g
    (fun a V x => by rw [hgcomp a V x, hψ]) hobj hhom i V x).symm

/-- **`pullbackPushforwardDesc` is the only such factorization**: a map of sheaves `F ⟶ H`
restricting to `g i` at every level is `pullbackPushforwardDesc`. -/
@[stacks 0EXJ "weak-system variant (Stacks 00VH finite coverings): uniqueness of the factorization \
  `pullbackPushforwardDesc`."]
public theorem eq_pullbackPushforwardDesc
    {C : Type w} [SmallCategory C] (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{u₁, u₂, w}) (u : ∀ i, D.C i ⥤ C)
    (hu : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j), D.u a ⋙ u i = u j)
    (hobj : ∀ X : C, ∃ (i : D.I) (Y : D.C i), (u i).obj Y = X)
    (hhom :
      ∀ (i : D.I) (X Y : D.C i) (f : (u i).obj X ⟶ (u i).obj Y),
        ∃ (j : D.I) (a : j ⟶ i) (g : (D.u a).obj X ⟶ (D.u a).obj Y),
          (u j).map g =
            eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) X) ≫ f ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) Y).symm)
    (_hhom_inj :
      ∀ (i : D.I) (X Y : D.C i) (g₁ g₂ : X ⟶ Y),
        (u i).map g₁ = (u i).map g₂ → ∃ (j : D.I) (a : j ⟶ i), (D.u a).map g₁ = (D.u a).map g₂)
    (K : Precoverage C)
    (_hK :
      ∀ (X : C) (R : Presieve X),
        R ∈ K X ↔
          ∃ (i : D.I) (Y : D.C i) (h : (u i).obj Y = X) (S : Presieve Y),
            S ∈ (D.J i).toPrecoverage Y ∧ S ∈ Precoverage.finite (D.C i) Y ∧ R = h ▸ S.map (u i))
    -- the sheaf `F` on `C`, and the canonical maps `φ_a : f_a^{-1}f_{i,*}F → f_{j,*}F` in
    -- adjoint form: `ψ a` is the identity `f_{i,*}F → f_{a,*}f_{j,*}F`
    (F : Sheaf K.toGrothendieck (Type w))
    (ψ : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i), (u i).op ⋙ F.obj ⟶ (D.u a).op ⋙ ((u j).op ⋙ F.obj))
    (hψ :
      ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i) (V : D.C i) (x : F.obj.obj (op ((u i).obj V))),
        (ψ a).app (op V) x =
          F.obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) V).symm)) x)
    -- a sheaf `H` on `C` and a family of maps `f_{i,*}F → f_{i,*}H` compatible with the `φ_a`
    (H : Sheaf K.toGrothendieck (Type w))
    (g : ∀ i, (u i).op ⋙ F.obj ⟶ (u i).op ⋙ H.obj)
    (hgcomp :
      ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i) (V : D.C i) (x : F.obj.obj (op ((u i).obj V))),
        (g i).app (op V) x =
          H.obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) V)))
            ((g j).app (op ((D.u a).obj V)) ((ψ a).app (op V) x)))
    (y : F ⟶ H)
    (hy : ∀ (i : D.I) (V : D.C i) (x : F.obj.obj (op ((u i).obj V))),
      (g i).app (op V) x = y.hom.app (op ((u i).obj V)) x) :
    y = pullbackPushforwardDesc D u hu hobj hhom _hhom_inj K _hK F ψ hψ H g hgcomp :=
  Sheaf.hom_ext (Stacks.WeakSites.ColimitPresheafDescent.eq_natTrans D u hu g
    (fun a V x => by rw [hgcomp a V x, hψ]) hobj hhom y.hom hy)

end InverseSystemOfFiniteSites

/-- **A sheaf on a colimit of sites is the colimit of the pullbacks of its pushforwards.** In the
situation of Stacks 0A34, let the functors `u i : D.C i ⥤ C` exhibit the small category `C` as the
colimit of the `D.C i` (`hu`, `hobj`, `hhom`, `hhom_inj`) and let `K` be the collection of
coverings of `C` of Stacks 09YL (`hK`), so that each `u i` defines a morphism of sites
`f_i : C → C_i` (Stacks 0A35).

Let `F` be a sheaf of sets on `C` and, for `a : j ⟶ i`, let `ψ a` be the adjoint of the canonical
map `φ_a : f_a^{-1}f_{i, *}F → f_{j, *}F`, that is the identity
`f_{i, *}F → f_{a, *}f_{j, *}F` (`hψ`; the two presheaves are equal because
`D.u a ⋙ u j = u i`).

Then the `φ_a` satisfy the cocycle condition `φ_{b ∘ a} = φ_b ∘ f_b^{-1}φ_a` of Stacks 09YN, and
`F = colim_i f_i^{-1}f_{i, *}F` with the counits as structure maps: for every sheaf `H` on `C`,
every family of maps `f_{i, *}F → f_{i, *}H` compatible with the `φ_a` consists of the
restrictions of a unique map of sheaves `F ⟶ H`.

This packages `cocycle_pullback_pushforward_of_colimit` with the universal property of
`pullbackPushforwardDesc`; that map is the factorization the existential asserts. -/
public theorem InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.isColimit_pullback_pushforward_of_colimit {C : Type w}
    [SmallCategory C] (D : InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.{u₁, u₂, w}) (u : ∀ i, D.C i ⥤ C)
    (hu : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j), D.u a ⋙ u i = u j)
    (hobj : ∀ X : C, ∃ (i : D.I) (Y : D.C i), (u i).obj Y = X)
    (hhom :
      ∀ (i : D.I) (X Y : D.C i) (f : (u i).obj X ⟶ (u i).obj Y),
        ∃ (j : D.I) (a : j ⟶ i) (g : (D.u a).obj X ⟶ (D.u a).obj Y),
          (u j).map g =
            eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) X) ≫ f ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) Y).symm)
    (_hhom_inj :
      ∀ (i : D.I) (X Y : D.C i) (g₁ g₂ : X ⟶ Y),
        (u i).map g₁ = (u i).map g₂ → ∃ (j : D.I) (a : j ⟶ i), (D.u a).map g₁ = (D.u a).map g₂)
    (K : Precoverage C)
    (_hK :
      ∀ (X : C) (R : Presieve X),
        R ∈ K X ↔
          ∃ (i : D.I) (Y : D.C i) (h : (u i).obj Y = X) (S : Presieve Y),
            S ∈ (D.J i).toPrecoverage Y ∧ S ∈ Precoverage.finite (D.C i) Y ∧ R = h ▸ S.map (u i))
    -- the sheaf `F` on `C`, and the canonical maps `φ_a : f_a^{-1}f_{i,*}F → f_{j,*}F` in
    -- adjoint form: `ψ a` is the identity `f_{i,*}F → f_{a,*}f_{j,*}F`
    (F : Sheaf K.toGrothendieck (Type w))
    (ψ : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i), (u i).op ⋙ F.obj ⟶ (D.u a).op ⋙ ((u j).op ⋙ F.obj))
    (hψ :
      ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i) (V : D.C i) (x : F.obj.obj (op ((u i).obj V))),
        (ψ a).app (op V) x =
          F.obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) V).symm)) x) :
    -- the cocycle condition `φ_{b ∘ a} = φ_b ∘ f_b^{-1}φ_a` of Stacks 09YN
    (∀ {i j k : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i) (b : k ⟶ j) (V : D.C i) (x : F.obj.obj (op ((u i).obj V))),
        (ψ (b ≫ a)).app (op V) x =
          ((u k).op ⋙ F.obj).map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (D.comp b a) V).symm))
            ((ψ b).app (op ((D.u a).obj V)) ((ψ a).app (op V) x))) ∧
      -- `F = colim_i f_i^{-1}f_{i,*}F`, with the counits `f_i^{-1}f_{i,*}F ⟶ F` as structure
      -- maps: every compatible family of maps to a sheaf `H` factors uniquely through them
      ∀ (H : Sheaf K.toGrothendieck (Type w)) (g : ∀ i, (u i).op ⋙ F.obj ⟶ (u i).op ⋙ H.obj),
        (∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i) (V : D.C i) (x : F.obj.obj (op ((u i).obj V))),
            (g i).app (op V) x =
              H.obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) V)))
                ((g j).app (op ((D.u a).obj V)) ((ψ a).app (op V) x))) →
          ∃! h : F ⟶ H,
            ∀ (i : D.I) (V : D.C i) (x : F.obj.obj (op ((u i).obj V))),
              (g i).app (op V) x = h.hom.app (op ((u i).obj V)) x :=
  ⟨fun a b V x =>
      InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.cocycle_pullback_pushforward_of_colimit D u hu hobj hhom _hhom_inj
        K _hK F ψ hψ a b V x,
    fun H g hgcomp =>
      ⟨InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.pullbackPushforwardDesc D u hu hobj hhom _hhom_inj K _hK F ψ hψ H
          g hgcomp,
        InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.pullbackPushforwardDesc_app D u hu hobj hhom _hhom_inj K _hK F
          ψ hψ H g hgcomp,
        InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.eq_pullbackPushforwardDesc D u hu hobj hhom _hhom_inj K _hK F
          ψ hψ H g hgcomp⟩⟩


/-! ### The special case of a system whose covering sieves are finitely generated

`InverseSystemOfSites` (Stacks 0A34 with the covering sieves finitely *generated*) is the special
case of `InverseSystemOfFiniteSites` in which `finiteCoverings` is strengthened, the two structures
carrying the same record-level data; `InverseSystemOfSites.toInverseSystemOfFiniteSites` is the
coercion. Each result below is therefore the general result of this file specialised along that
coercion, and is stated here rather than alongside the strong structure because the general form it
delegates to is proved here. -/

/-- **Sections of a colimit of sheaves on a colimit of sites.** In the situation of Stacks 0A34,
let the functors `u i : D.C i ⥤ C` exhibit the small category `C` as the colimit of the `D.C i`
(`hu`, `hobj`, `hhom`, `hhom_inj`) and let `K` be the collection of coverings of `C` of
Stacks 09YL (`hK`), so that each `u i` defines a morphism of sites `f_i : C → C_i`
(Stacks 0A35).

Let `F i` be a sheaf of sets on `(D.C i, D.J i)` for every `i`, and for `a : j ⟶ i` let
`ψ a : F i ⟶ f_{a,*}F j` be the adjoint of a map `φ_a : f_a^{-1}F_i → F_j` of sheaves on `D.C j`,
subject to the cocycle condition `hψ`. Let `G` be the colimit `colim_i f_i^{-1}F_i`, presented by
its universal property: `ι i` is the adjoint of the structure map `f_i^{-1}F_i ⟶ G` (`hι`) and
every compatible family of maps to a sheaf `H` on `C` factors uniquely through it (`hG`).

Then for every object `X` of `D.C i` the sections of `G` over `u_i(X)` are the filtered colimit
over the arrows `a : j ⟶ i` of the sections of `F j` over `u_a(X)`: the canonical maps `ρ a`
(`hρ`) are jointly surjective, and two sections of `F j` over `u_a(X)` with the same image under
`ρ a` agree after applying `ψ b` for some `b : k ⟶ j`. -/
@[stacks 09YN "The sections over `u_i(X_i)` of the colimit `colim f_i^{-1}F_i` of a system of
  sheaves on an inverse system of sites are the filtered colimit of the sections `F_j(u_a(X_i))`
  over the arrows `a : j → i`."]
public theorem InverseSystemOfSites.sections_colimit_pullback_of_colimit {C : Type w}
    [SmallCategory C] (D : InverseSystemOfSites.{u₁, u₂, w}) (u : ∀ i, D.C i ⥤ C)
    (hu : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j), D.u a ⋙ u i = u j)
    (hobj : ∀ X : C, ∃ (i : D.I) (Y : D.C i), (u i).obj Y = X)
    (hhom :
      ∀ (i : D.I) (X Y : D.C i) (f : (u i).obj X ⟶ (u i).obj Y),
        ∃ (j : D.I) (a : j ⟶ i) (g : (D.u a).obj X ⟶ (D.u a).obj Y),
          (u j).map g =
            eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) X) ≫ f ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) Y).symm)
    (hhom_inj :
      ∀ (i : D.I) (X Y : D.C i) (g₁ g₂ : X ⟶ Y),
        (u i).map g₁ = (u i).map g₂ → ∃ (j : D.I) (a : j ⟶ i), (D.u a).map g₁ = (D.u a).map g₂)
    (K : Precoverage C)
    (hK :
      ∀ (X : C) (R : Presieve X),
        R ∈ K X ↔
          ∃ (i : D.I) (Y : D.C i) (h : (u i).obj Y = X) (S : Presieve Y),
            S ∈ (D.J i).toPrecoverage Y ∧ S ∈ Precoverage.finite (D.C i) Y ∧ R = h ▸ S.map (u i))
    -- the sheaves `F i` and, in adjoint form, the maps `φ_a : f_a^{-1}F_i → F_j`
    (F : ∀ i, Sheaf (D.J i) (Type w))
    (ψ : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i), (F i).obj ⟶ (D.u a).op ⋙ (F j).obj)
    -- the cocycle condition `φ_{b ∘ a} = φ_b ∘ f_b^{-1}φ_a`
    (hψ :
      ∀ {i j k : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i) (b : k ⟶ j) (V : D.C i) (x : (F i).obj.obj (op V)),
        (ψ (b ≫ a)).app (op V) x =
          (F k).obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (D.comp b a) V).symm))
            ((ψ b).app (op ((D.u a).obj V)) ((ψ a).app (op V) x)))
    -- `G = colim_i f_i^{-1}F_i`, presented by its universal property
    (G : Sheaf K.toGrothendieck (Type w)) (ι : ∀ i, (F i).obj ⟶ (u i).op ⋙ G.obj)
    (hι :
      ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i) (V : D.C i) (x : (F i).obj.obj (op V)),
        (ι i).app (op V) x =
          G.obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) V)))
            ((ι j).app (op ((D.u a).obj V)) ((ψ a).app (op V) x)))
    (hG :
      ∀ (H : Sheaf K.toGrothendieck (Type w)) (g : ∀ i, (F i).obj ⟶ (u i).op ⋙ H.obj),
        (∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i) (V : D.C i) (x : (F i).obj.obj (op V)),
            (g i).app (op V) x =
              H.obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) V)))
                ((g j).app (op ((D.u a).obj V)) ((ψ a).app (op V) x))) →
          ∃! h : G ⟶ H,
            ∀ (i : D.I) (V : D.C i) (x : (F i).obj.obj (op V)),
              (g i).app (op V) x = h.hom.app (op ((u i).obj V)) ((ι i).app (op V) x))
    (i : D.I) (X : D.C i)
    -- the canonical maps `F_j(u_a(X)) → G(u_i(X))`
    (ρ :
      ∀ {j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i), (F j).obj.obj (op ((D.u a).obj X)) → G.obj.obj (op ((u i).obj X)))
    (hρ :
      ∀ {j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i) (t : (F j).obj.obj (op ((D.u a).obj X))),
        ρ a t =
          G.obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) X)))
            ((ι j).app (op ((D.u a).obj X)) t)) :
    -- every section of `G` over `u_i(X)` comes from some level below `i`
    (∀ s : G.obj.obj (op ((u i).obj X)),
        ∃ (j : D.I) (a : j ⟶ i) (t : (F j).obj.obj (op ((D.u a).obj X))), ρ a t = s) ∧
      -- two sections with the same image agree at a further level
      ∀ (j : D.I) (a : j ⟶ i) (t t' : (F j).obj.obj (op ((D.u a).obj X))),
        ρ a t = ρ a t' →
          ∃ (k : D.I) (b : k ⟶ j),
            (ψ b).app (op ((D.u a).obj X)) t = (ψ b).app (op ((D.u a).obj X)) t' :=
  InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.sections_colimit_pullback_of_colimit D.toInverseSystemOfFiniteSites u
    hu hobj hhom hhom_inj K hK F ψ hψ G ι hι hG i X ρ hρ

/-- **The colimit of an inverse system of sites.** In the situation of Stacks 0A34, let the
functors `u i : D.C i ⥤ C` exhibit the small category `C` as the colimit of the `D.C i` (`hu`,
`hobj`, `hhom`, `hhom_inj`) and let `K` be the collection of coverings of `C` of Stacks 09YL, the
images under the `u i` of the finite coverings of the `D.C i` (`hK`).

Then each `u i` defines a morphism of sites `f_i : C → C_i` between `(C, K.toGrothendieck)` and
`(D.C i, D.J i)`: it is continuous and `f_i^{-1}` is exact (Stacks 00X1). Moreover, for every
object `U` of `D.C i` and every sheaf of sets `F` on `D.C i`, the canonical maps
`θ a : f_a^{-1}F(u_a U) → f_i^{-1}F(u_i U)`, indexed by the arrows `a : j ⟶ i` of `D.I`, exhibit
`f_i^{-1}F(u_i U)` as their filtered colimit: every section of `f_i^{-1}F` over `u_i U` is `θ a t`
for some `a` and some section `t` of `f_a^{-1}F` over `u_a U`, and two sections of `f_a^{-1}F` over
`u_a U` with the same image under `θ a` agree after pullback along `D.u b` for some `b : k ⟶ j`.
This is equation (09YM) of the source. -/
@[stacks 0A35 "The functors `u_i` from the members of an inverse system of sites to its colimit
  define morphisms of sites, and the sections of `f_i^{-1}F` over `u_i(U_i)` are the filtered
  colimit of the sections of `f_a^{-1}F` over `u_a(U_i)`."]
public theorem InverseSystemOfSites.exists_isMorphismOfSites_sections_pullback_of_colimit
    {C : Type w} [SmallCategory C] (D : InverseSystemOfSites.{u₁, u₂, w}) (u : ∀ i, D.C i ⥤ C)
    (hu : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j), D.u a ⋙ u i = u j)
    (hobj : ∀ X : C, ∃ (i : D.I) (Y : D.C i), (u i).obj Y = X)
    (hhom :
      ∀ (i : D.I) (X Y : D.C i) (f : (u i).obj X ⟶ (u i).obj Y),
        ∃ (j : D.I) (a : j ⟶ i) (g : (D.u a).obj X ⟶ (D.u a).obj Y),
          (u j).map g =
            eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) X) ≫ f ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) Y).symm)
    (hhom_inj :
      ∀ (i : D.I) (X Y : D.C i) (g₁ g₂ : X ⟶ Y),
        (u i).map g₁ = (u i).map g₂ → ∃ (j : D.I) (a : j ⟶ i), (D.u a).map g₁ = (D.u a).map g₂)
    (K : Precoverage C)
    (hK :
      ∀ (X : C) (R : Presieve X),
        R ∈ K X ↔
          ∃ (i : D.I) (Y : D.C i) (h : (u i).obj Y = X) (S : Presieve Y),
            S ∈ (D.J i).toPrecoverage Y ∧ S ∈ Precoverage.finite (D.C i) Y ∧ R = h ▸ S.map (u i)) :
    ∃ hf : ∀ i, (u i).IsMorphismOfSites (D.J i) K.toGrothendieck,
      haveI _hcont : ∀ i, (u i).IsContinuous (D.J i) K.toGrothendieck := fun i =>
        (hf i).isContinuous
      haveI _hcontu : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j), (D.u a).IsContinuous (D.J j) (D.J i) := fun a =>
        D.continuous a
      ∀ (i : D.I) (U : D.C i) (F : Sheaf (D.J i) (Type w))
        (θ :
          ∀ {j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i),
            (((D.u a).sheafPullback (Type w) (D.J i) (D.J j)).obj F).obj.obj (op ((D.u a).obj U)) →
              (((u i).sheafPullback (Type w) (D.J i) K.toGrothendieck).obj F).obj.obj
                (op ((u i).obj U))),
        (∀ {j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i),
            θ a =
              (((D.u a).sheafPushforwardContinuous (Type w) (D.J i) (D.J j)).map
                      ((((D.u a).sheafAdjunctionContinuous (Type w) (D.J i) (D.J j)).homEquiv F
                            (((u j).sheafPushforwardContinuous (Type w) (D.J j)
                                  K.toGrothendieck).obj
                              (((u i).sheafPullback (Type w) (D.J i) K.toGrothendieck).obj
                                F))).symm
                        (((u i).sheafAdjunctionContinuous (Type w) (D.J i)
                                K.toGrothendieck).unit.app
                            F ≫
                          (Functor.sheafPushforwardContinuousComp' (eqToIso (hu a)) (Type w)
                                (D.J i) (D.J j) K.toGrothendieck).inv.app
                            _)) ≫
                    (Functor.sheafPushforwardContinuousComp' (eqToIso (hu a)) (Type w) (D.J i)
                          (D.J j) K.toGrothendieck).hom.app
                      _).hom.app
                (op U)) →
          (∀ s :
              (((u i).sheafPullback (Type w) (D.J i) K.toGrothendieck).obj F).obj.obj
                (op ((u i).obj U)),
              ∃ (j : D.I) (a : j ⟶ i) (t :
                (((D.u a).sheafPullback (Type w) (D.J i) (D.J j)).obj F).obj.obj
                  (op ((D.u a).obj U))),
                θ a t = s) ∧
            ∀ (j : D.I) (a : j ⟶ i)
              (t t' :
                (((D.u a).sheafPullback (Type w) (D.J i) (D.J j)).obj F).obj.obj
                  (op ((D.u a).obj U))),
              θ a t = θ a t' →
                ∃ (k : D.I) (b : k ⟶ j),
                  (((D.u b).sheafAdjunctionContinuous (Type w) (D.J j) (D.J k)).unit.app
                          (((D.u a).sheafPullback (Type w) (D.J i) (D.J j)).obj F)).hom.app
                      (op ((D.u a).obj U)) t =
                    (((D.u b).sheafAdjunctionContinuous (Type w) (D.J j) (D.J k)).unit.app
                          (((D.u a).sheafPullback (Type w) (D.J i) (D.J j)).obj F)).hom.app
                      (op ((D.u a).obj U)) t' :=
  InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.exists_isMorphismOfSites_sections_pullback_of_colimit
    D.toInverseSystemOfFiniteSites u hu hobj hhom hhom_inj K hK

/-- **The cocycle condition of Stacks 09YN.** The canonical maps
`φ_a : f_a^{-1}f_{i, *}F → f_{j, *}F`, in the adjoint form `ψ`, satisfy
`φ_{b ∘ a} = φ_b ∘ f_b^{-1}φ_a`: each `ψ a` is the transport along `D.u a ⋙ u j = u i`, and the
transports compose. -/
@[stacks 0EXJ "the cocycle condition `φ_{b ∘ a} = φ_b ∘ f_b^{-1}φ_a` of Stacks 09YN satisfied by
  the counits `φ_a : f_a^{-1}f_{i,*}F → f_{j,*}F`."]
public theorem InverseSystemOfSites.cocycle_pullback_pushforward_of_colimit
    {C : Type w} [SmallCategory C] (D : InverseSystemOfSites.{u₁, u₂, w}) (u : ∀ i, D.C i ⥤ C)
    (hu : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j), D.u a ⋙ u i = u j)
    (_hobj : ∀ X : C, ∃ (i : D.I) (Y : D.C i), (u i).obj Y = X)
    (_hhom :
      ∀ (i : D.I) (X Y : D.C i) (f : (u i).obj X ⟶ (u i).obj Y),
        ∃ (j : D.I) (a : j ⟶ i) (g : (D.u a).obj X ⟶ (D.u a).obj Y),
          (u j).map g =
            eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) X) ≫ f ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) Y).symm)
    (_hhom_inj :
      ∀ (i : D.I) (X Y : D.C i) (g₁ g₂ : X ⟶ Y),
        (u i).map g₁ = (u i).map g₂ → ∃ (j : D.I) (a : j ⟶ i), (D.u a).map g₁ = (D.u a).map g₂)
    (K : Precoverage C)
    (_hK :
      ∀ (X : C) (R : Presieve X),
        R ∈ K X ↔
          ∃ (i : D.I) (Y : D.C i) (h : (u i).obj Y = X) (S : Presieve Y),
            S ∈ (D.J i).toPrecoverage Y ∧ S ∈ Precoverage.finite (D.C i) Y ∧ R = h ▸ S.map (u i))
    -- the sheaf `F` on `C`, and the canonical maps `φ_a : f_a^{-1}f_{i,*}F → f_{j,*}F` in
    -- adjoint form: `ψ a` is the identity `f_{i,*}F → f_{a,*}f_{j,*}F`
    (F : Sheaf K.toGrothendieck (Type w))
    (ψ : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i), (u i).op ⋙ F.obj ⟶ (D.u a).op ⋙ ((u j).op ⋙ F.obj))
    (hψ :
      ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i) (V : D.C i) (x : F.obj.obj (op ((u i).obj V))),
        (ψ a).app (op V) x =
          F.obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) V).symm)) x)
    {i j k : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i) (b : k ⟶ j) (V : D.C i)
    (x : F.obj.obj (op ((u i).obj V))) :
    (ψ (b ≫ a)).app (op V) x =
      ((u k).op ⋙ F.obj).map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (D.comp b a) V).symm))
        ((ψ b).app (op ((D.u a).obj V)) ((ψ a).app (op V) x)) :=
  InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.cocycle_pullback_pushforward_of_colimit D.toInverseSystemOfFiniteSites
    u hu _hobj _hhom _hhom_inj K _hK F ψ hψ a b V x

/-- **The factorization of a compatible family through the counits.** Writing
`F = colim_i f_i^{-1}f_{i, *}F` with the counits as structure maps, this is the map of sheaves
`F ⟶ H` whose restriction to the level `i` is `g i`. It is built level by level: a presentation
`u_i(V) = X` of an object `X` of `C` carries the section `g i` over `V`, and the compatibility
`hgcomp` makes the result independent of the presentation chosen. -/
@[stacks 0EXJ "the map `F ⟶ H` that a compatible family `g` factors through; its defining property
  is `pullbackPushforwardDesc_app` and its uniqueness `eq_pullbackPushforwardDesc`.", no_expose]
public noncomputable def InverseSystemOfSites.pullbackPushforwardDesc
    {C : Type w} [SmallCategory C] (D : InverseSystemOfSites.{u₁, u₂, w}) (u : ∀ i, D.C i ⥤ C)
    (hu : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j), D.u a ⋙ u i = u j)
    (hobj : ∀ X : C, ∃ (i : D.I) (Y : D.C i), (u i).obj Y = X)
    (hhom :
      ∀ (i : D.I) (X Y : D.C i) (f : (u i).obj X ⟶ (u i).obj Y),
        ∃ (j : D.I) (a : j ⟶ i) (g : (D.u a).obj X ⟶ (D.u a).obj Y),
          (u j).map g =
            eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) X) ≫ f ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) Y).symm)
    (_hhom_inj :
      ∀ (i : D.I) (X Y : D.C i) (g₁ g₂ : X ⟶ Y),
        (u i).map g₁ = (u i).map g₂ → ∃ (j : D.I) (a : j ⟶ i), (D.u a).map g₁ = (D.u a).map g₂)
    (K : Precoverage C)
    (_hK :
      ∀ (X : C) (R : Presieve X),
        R ∈ K X ↔
          ∃ (i : D.I) (Y : D.C i) (h : (u i).obj Y = X) (S : Presieve Y),
            S ∈ (D.J i).toPrecoverage Y ∧ S ∈ Precoverage.finite (D.C i) Y ∧ R = h ▸ S.map (u i))
    -- the sheaf `F` on `C`, and the canonical maps `φ_a : f_a^{-1}f_{i,*}F → f_{j,*}F` in
    -- adjoint form: `ψ a` is the identity `f_{i,*}F → f_{a,*}f_{j,*}F`
    (F : Sheaf K.toGrothendieck (Type w))
    (ψ : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i), (u i).op ⋙ F.obj ⟶ (D.u a).op ⋙ ((u j).op ⋙ F.obj))
    (hψ :
      ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i) (V : D.C i) (x : F.obj.obj (op ((u i).obj V))),
        (ψ a).app (op V) x =
          F.obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) V).symm)) x)
    -- a sheaf `H` on `C` and a family of maps `f_{i,*}F → f_{i,*}H` compatible with the `φ_a`
    (H : Sheaf K.toGrothendieck (Type w))
    (g : ∀ i, (u i).op ⋙ F.obj ⟶ (u i).op ⋙ H.obj)
    (hgcomp :
      ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i) (V : D.C i) (x : F.obj.obj (op ((u i).obj V))),
        (g i).app (op V) x =
          H.obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) V)))
            ((g j).app (op ((D.u a).obj V)) ((ψ a).app (op V) x)))
    : F ⟶ H :=
  InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.pullbackPushforwardDesc D.toInverseSystemOfFiniteSites u hu hobj hhom
    _hhom_inj K _hK F ψ hψ H g hgcomp

/-- **`pullbackPushforwardDesc` restricts to `g i` at every level**: it is a factorization of the
family `g` through the counits. -/
@[stacks 0EXJ "`pullbackPushforwardDesc` restricts to `g i` at every level."]
public theorem InverseSystemOfSites.pullbackPushforwardDesc_app
    {C : Type w} [SmallCategory C] (D : InverseSystemOfSites.{u₁, u₂, w}) (u : ∀ i, D.C i ⥤ C)
    (hu : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j), D.u a ⋙ u i = u j)
    (hobj : ∀ X : C, ∃ (i : D.I) (Y : D.C i), (u i).obj Y = X)
    (hhom :
      ∀ (i : D.I) (X Y : D.C i) (f : (u i).obj X ⟶ (u i).obj Y),
        ∃ (j : D.I) (a : j ⟶ i) (g : (D.u a).obj X ⟶ (D.u a).obj Y),
          (u j).map g =
            eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) X) ≫ f ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) Y).symm)
    (_hhom_inj :
      ∀ (i : D.I) (X Y : D.C i) (g₁ g₂ : X ⟶ Y),
        (u i).map g₁ = (u i).map g₂ → ∃ (j : D.I) (a : j ⟶ i), (D.u a).map g₁ = (D.u a).map g₂)
    (K : Precoverage C)
    (_hK :
      ∀ (X : C) (R : Presieve X),
        R ∈ K X ↔
          ∃ (i : D.I) (Y : D.C i) (h : (u i).obj Y = X) (S : Presieve Y),
            S ∈ (D.J i).toPrecoverage Y ∧ S ∈ Precoverage.finite (D.C i) Y ∧ R = h ▸ S.map (u i))
    -- the sheaf `F` on `C`, and the canonical maps `φ_a : f_a^{-1}f_{i,*}F → f_{j,*}F` in
    -- adjoint form: `ψ a` is the identity `f_{i,*}F → f_{a,*}f_{j,*}F`
    (F : Sheaf K.toGrothendieck (Type w))
    (ψ : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i), (u i).op ⋙ F.obj ⟶ (D.u a).op ⋙ ((u j).op ⋙ F.obj))
    (hψ :
      ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i) (V : D.C i) (x : F.obj.obj (op ((u i).obj V))),
        (ψ a).app (op V) x =
          F.obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) V).symm)) x)
    -- a sheaf `H` on `C` and a family of maps `f_{i,*}F → f_{i,*}H` compatible with the `φ_a`
    (H : Sheaf K.toGrothendieck (Type w))
    (g : ∀ i, (u i).op ⋙ F.obj ⟶ (u i).op ⋙ H.obj)
    (hgcomp :
      ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i) (V : D.C i) (x : F.obj.obj (op ((u i).obj V))),
        (g i).app (op V) x =
          H.obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) V)))
            ((g j).app (op ((D.u a).obj V)) ((ψ a).app (op V) x)))
    (i : D.I) (V : D.C i) (x : F.obj.obj (op ((u i).obj V))) :
    (g i).app (op V) x =
      (pullbackPushforwardDesc D u hu hobj hhom _hhom_inj K _hK F ψ hψ H g hgcomp).hom.app
        (op ((u i).obj V)) x :=
  InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.pullbackPushforwardDesc_app D.toInverseSystemOfFiniteSites u hu hobj
    hhom _hhom_inj K _hK F ψ hψ H g hgcomp i V x

/-- **`pullbackPushforwardDesc` is the only such factorization**: a map of sheaves `F ⟶ H`
restricting to `g i` at every level is `pullbackPushforwardDesc`. -/
@[stacks 0EXJ "uniqueness of the factorization `pullbackPushforwardDesc`."]
public theorem InverseSystemOfSites.eq_pullbackPushforwardDesc
    {C : Type w} [SmallCategory C] (D : InverseSystemOfSites.{u₁, u₂, w}) (u : ∀ i, D.C i ⥤ C)
    (hu : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j), D.u a ⋙ u i = u j)
    (hobj : ∀ X : C, ∃ (i : D.I) (Y : D.C i), (u i).obj Y = X)
    (hhom :
      ∀ (i : D.I) (X Y : D.C i) (f : (u i).obj X ⟶ (u i).obj Y),
        ∃ (j : D.I) (a : j ⟶ i) (g : (D.u a).obj X ⟶ (D.u a).obj Y),
          (u j).map g =
            eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) X) ≫ f ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) Y).symm)
    (_hhom_inj :
      ∀ (i : D.I) (X Y : D.C i) (g₁ g₂ : X ⟶ Y),
        (u i).map g₁ = (u i).map g₂ → ∃ (j : D.I) (a : j ⟶ i), (D.u a).map g₁ = (D.u a).map g₂)
    (K : Precoverage C)
    (_hK :
      ∀ (X : C) (R : Presieve X),
        R ∈ K X ↔
          ∃ (i : D.I) (Y : D.C i) (h : (u i).obj Y = X) (S : Presieve Y),
            S ∈ (D.J i).toPrecoverage Y ∧ S ∈ Precoverage.finite (D.C i) Y ∧ R = h ▸ S.map (u i))
    -- the sheaf `F` on `C`, and the canonical maps `φ_a : f_a^{-1}f_{i,*}F → f_{j,*}F` in
    -- adjoint form: `ψ a` is the identity `f_{i,*}F → f_{a,*}f_{j,*}F`
    (F : Sheaf K.toGrothendieck (Type w))
    (ψ : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i), (u i).op ⋙ F.obj ⟶ (D.u a).op ⋙ ((u j).op ⋙ F.obj))
    (hψ :
      ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i) (V : D.C i) (x : F.obj.obj (op ((u i).obj V))),
        (ψ a).app (op V) x =
          F.obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) V).symm)) x)
    -- a sheaf `H` on `C` and a family of maps `f_{i,*}F → f_{i,*}H` compatible with the `φ_a`
    (H : Sheaf K.toGrothendieck (Type w))
    (g : ∀ i, (u i).op ⋙ F.obj ⟶ (u i).op ⋙ H.obj)
    (hgcomp :
      ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i) (V : D.C i) (x : F.obj.obj (op ((u i).obj V))),
        (g i).app (op V) x =
          H.obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) V)))
            ((g j).app (op ((D.u a).obj V)) ((ψ a).app (op V) x)))
    (y : F ⟶ H)
    (hy : ∀ (i : D.I) (V : D.C i) (x : F.obj.obj (op ((u i).obj V))),
      (g i).app (op V) x = y.hom.app (op ((u i).obj V)) x) :
    y = pullbackPushforwardDesc D u hu hobj hhom _hhom_inj K _hK F ψ hψ H g hgcomp :=
  InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.eq_pullbackPushforwardDesc D.toInverseSystemOfFiniteSites u hu hobj
    hhom _hhom_inj K _hK F ψ hψ H g hgcomp y hy

/-- **A sheaf on a colimit of sites is the colimit of the pullbacks of its pushforwards.** In the
situation of Stacks 0A34, let the functors `u i : D.C i ⥤ C` exhibit the small category `C` as the
colimit of the `D.C i` (`hu`, `hobj`, `hhom`, `hhom_inj`) and let `K` be the collection of
coverings of `C` of Stacks 09YL (`hK`), so that each `u i` defines a morphism of sites
`f_i : C → C_i` (Stacks 0A35).

Let `F` be a sheaf of sets on `C` and, for `a : j ⟶ i`, let `ψ a` be the adjoint of the canonical
map `φ_a : f_a^{-1}f_{i, *}F → f_{j, *}F`, that is the identity
`f_{i, *}F → f_{a, *}f_{j, *}F` (`hψ`; the two presheaves are equal because
`D.u a ⋙ u j = u i`).

Then the `φ_a` satisfy the cocycle condition `φ_{b ∘ a} = φ_b ∘ f_b^{-1}φ_a` of Stacks 09YN, and
`F = colim_i f_i^{-1}f_{i, *}F` with the counits as structure maps: for every sheaf `H` on `C`,
every family of maps `f_{i, *}F → f_{i, *}H` compatible with the `φ_a` consists of the
restrictions of a unique map of sheaves `F ⟶ H`.

This packages `cocycle_pullback_pushforward_of_colimit` with the universal property of
`pullbackPushforwardDesc`; that map is the factorization the existential asserts. -/
public theorem InverseSystemOfSites.isColimit_pullback_pushforward_of_colimit {C : Type w}
    [SmallCategory C] (D : InverseSystemOfSites.{u₁, u₂, w}) (u : ∀ i, D.C i ⥤ C)
    (hu : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : i ⟶ j), D.u a ⋙ u i = u j)
    (hobj : ∀ X : C, ∃ (i : D.I) (Y : D.C i), (u i).obj Y = X)
    (hhom :
      ∀ (i : D.I) (X Y : D.C i) (f : (u i).obj X ⟶ (u i).obj Y),
        ∃ (j : D.I) (a : j ⟶ i) (g : (D.u a).obj X ⟶ (D.u a).obj Y),
          (u j).map g =
            eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) X) ≫ f ≫ eqToHom (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) Y).symm)
    (_hhom_inj :
      ∀ (i : D.I) (X Y : D.C i) (g₁ g₂ : X ⟶ Y),
        (u i).map g₁ = (u i).map g₂ → ∃ (j : D.I) (a : j ⟶ i), (D.u a).map g₁ = (D.u a).map g₂)
    (K : Precoverage C)
    (_hK :
      ∀ (X : C) (R : Presieve X),
        R ∈ K X ↔
          ∃ (i : D.I) (Y : D.C i) (h : (u i).obj Y = X) (S : Presieve Y),
            S ∈ (D.J i).toPrecoverage Y ∧ S ∈ Precoverage.finite (D.C i) Y ∧ R = h ▸ S.map (u i))
    -- the sheaf `F` on `C`, and the canonical maps `φ_a : f_a^{-1}f_{i,*}F → f_{j,*}F` in
    -- adjoint form: `ψ a` is the identity `f_{i,*}F → f_{a,*}f_{j,*}F`
    (F : Sheaf K.toGrothendieck (Type w))
    (ψ : ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i), (u i).op ⋙ F.obj ⟶ (D.u a).op ⋙ ((u j).op ⋙ F.obj))
    (hψ :
      ∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i) (V : D.C i) (x : F.obj.obj (op ((u i).obj V))),
        (ψ a).app (op V) x =
          F.obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) V).symm)) x) :
    -- the cocycle condition `φ_{b ∘ a} = φ_b ∘ f_b^{-1}φ_a` of Stacks 09YN
    (∀ {i j k : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i) (b : k ⟶ j) (V : D.C i) (x : F.obj.obj (op ((u i).obj V))),
        (ψ (b ≫ a)).app (op V) x =
          ((u k).op ⋙ F.obj).map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (D.comp b a) V).symm))
            ((ψ b).app (op ((D.u a).obj V)) ((ψ a).app (op V) x))) ∧
      -- `F = colim_i f_i^{-1}f_{i,*}F`, with the counits `f_i^{-1}f_{i,*}F ⟶ F` as structure
      -- maps: every compatible family of maps to a sheaf `H` factors uniquely through them
      ∀ (H : Sheaf K.toGrothendieck (Type w)) (g : ∀ i, (u i).op ⋙ F.obj ⟶ (u i).op ⋙ H.obj),
        (∀ {i j : D.I} (a : j ⟶ i) (V : D.C i) (x : F.obj.obj (op ((u i).obj V))),
            (g i).app (op V) x =
              H.obj.map (eqToHom (congrArg op (Functor.congr_obj (hu a) V)))
                ((g j).app (op ((D.u a).obj V)) ((ψ a).app (op V) x))) →
          ∃! h : F ⟶ H,
            ∀ (i : D.I) (V : D.C i) (x : F.obj.obj (op ((u i).obj V))),
              (g i).app (op V) x = h.hom.app (op ((u i).obj V)) x :=
  InverseSystemOfFiniteSites.isColimit_pullback_pushforward_of_colimit
    D.toInverseSystemOfFiniteSites u hu hobj hhom _hhom_inj K _hK F ψ hψ
end

end

